and ruts in the drive are illustrative; the grade and the line of the jeep track are real.","Trees, shrubs, grass tufts and boulders are placed where WorldCover maps that cover; their size and number are illustrative.","The walking loop is a 18 m circle around the arrival point; it is not a mapped trail.","Trees within 100 m of the Kumrat Waterfall are left out so it can be seen; WorldCover 2021 maps tree cover there.","The fall is drawn on the real slope: no terrace is cut (terrace 0). Trees within 100 m of the fall are left out so it can be seen (WorldCover 2021 maps tree cover there). The stream line runs from a lip at DEM 2520 m down to a plunge pool at the foot (DEM 2400 m), about 210 m long and about 120 m of drop read from the Copernicus DEM (30 m DSM, approximate; the DSM smooths the chute and cannot show a lip, so the drop is an estimate and may be too large or small).","The gully is the DEM steepest-descent line through the slope above the valley floor. No stream is mapped in OSM here (the only mapped waterway in the box is the Panjkora River, about 200 m west), so the stream is not named and its line is not a surveyed one.","The gorge walls (two rows of displaced low-poly rock blocks, 6-14 m tall, spaced 7 m apart along the line, grey with lichen-green patches), the foam (four steps of translucent sheets with scrolling streaks), the spray at each step and at the pool, the plunge pool (a flat disc about 16 m across) and the 10-20 boulders of 1-3 m at the foot are illustrative paint.","The OSM waterfall node (waterway=waterfall, id 6534025186) is at 35.569517, 72.192008, 0.1 m from the place point, and is used as the landmark point.","The drive is the Kumrat valley road (OSM tertiary, ref S-16); the trailhead is its nearest mapped vertex to the fall, about 180 m away. The walk to the foot (about 110 m) is traced over the DEM.","The walk from the end of the jeep track follows the mapped OSM footpath for 0.0 km; the last 0.11 km is not mapped and is traced over the ground (easiest slope on the DEM).","The 35 buildings stand on their OSM footprints; their height (OSM levels where mapped, else one or two storeys), roofs and colours are illustrative, after visitors' photos.","Season colours, snow, ice and dawn mist are illustrative.","Traffic on the drive is illustrative: the vehicle kinds are those seen on Swat roads (Willys jeeps, Hilux, Suzuki vans, Mehran cars, CD70 motorbikes, Qingqi rickshaws, painted trucks); their number and movement are not counted."],"sources":[{"name":"Copernicus DEM GLO-30","use":"terrain heights","licence":"© DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA","url":"https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model"},{"name":"ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200","use":"trees, meadow, rock, snow","licence":"CC BY 4.0, © ESA WorldCover project 2021","url":"https://esa-worldcover.org"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap (waterfall node 6534025186, road S-16 way 303252801, Panjkora River, via the main API)","use":"the fall's position, the valley road and its trailhead, the river west of the fall","licence":"ODbL 1.0","url":"https://api.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=72.1620,35.5530,72.2220,35.5870"},{"name":"Copernicus DEM GLO-30 (DSM, 30 m)","use":"the chute, the drop and the ground under everything (measured, approximate)","licence":"Copernicus licence (free, attribution)","url":"https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap","use":"the Kumrat valley road (tertiary, no surface tag) to the point nearest the fall, the waterfall node, the Panjkora River and the lower valley","licence":"ODbL, © OpenStreetMap contributors","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}]}